00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.840
Well, it's changed my life twice really.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.070
When YouTube first came out I was not a creator
and more of a consumer.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:59.050
And it was just amazing to see the shift from
traditional media to new media.

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:03.610
You had these videos coming up, an video would
go viral and everyone would be talking about

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.610
it.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:07.230
It was just really exciting because there
was nothing like that at the time.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.200
We had these creators for the first time.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.470
There was Smosh and Lisa Nova, Kassem G, Daxflame...

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:21.010
The content that they were making was just
so much different than anything that you would

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:23.750
find on television or in the movies.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:29.280
So it was really cool to see that and it just
changed the way I looked at media.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.280
And then obviously it's changed my life again
more recently with me becoming a creator.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.350
It's allowed me to make the videos that I
want to make and have my own career off of

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:42.790
it which is amazing and before YouTube there
was just nothing like that.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:49.250
If it wasn't for YouTube and just online media
in general, I would probably be scraping through

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:55.810
